es.md","line":86},{"title":"Create IP Address records from allocated IPs","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/telecom-network-inventory/telecommunications-network-inventory/create-ip-address-records-from-allocated-ips.md","line":91},{"title":"CMDB relationships for IP address records","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/telecom-network-inventory/telecommunications-network-inventory/cmdb-relationships-for-ip-address-records.md","line":93},{"title":"IP Address form","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/telecom-network-inventory/telecommunications-network-inventory/ip-address-form.md","line":95},{"title":"Create an IP Subnetwork record","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/telecom-network-inventory/telecommunications-network-inventory/create-an-ip-subnetwork-record.md","line":97},{"title":"Telecommunications Network Inventory","target":"telecom-network-inventory","line":101},{"title":"Network Inventory Workspace","target":"exploring-network-inventory-workspace","line":102},{"title":"Inventory number allocation","target":"inventory_number_allocation","line":103},{"title":"Data model","target":"uses-for-network-inventory-data","line":104}],"metadata":{"title":"Create an IP Address record at subnet level","description":"Create a single IP Address record that represents an entire IP Subnetwork as one Configuration Item. The IP Address record uses the subnetwork’s CIDR as its value, rather than a single host address. This method is used when the subnetwork is bound to a service, port, customer, or interface as a single entity.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/telecom-network-inventory/telecommunications-network-inventory/create-an-ip-address-record-at-subnet-level.html","release":"australia","product":"Telecommunications Network Inv